      "description": "Sliced seared chicken with vivid herb chimichurri, roasted potatoes and zucchini",
      "servings": "2 servings",
      "totalTime": "PT40M",
      "ingredients": [
        "12 oz boneless skinless chicken",
        "12 oz potatoes, cut into 1-inch pieces",
        "2 zucchini, thickly sliced",
        "½ cup packed fresh parsley, finely chopped",
        "1 garlic clove, minced",
        "2 Tbsp red wine vinegar",
        "3 Tbsp olive oil, divided",
        "½ tsp dried oregano",
        "Pinch red pepper flakes",
        "Salt & black pepper"
      ],
      "steps": [
        "Heat oven to 425°F. Toss potatoes with 1 Tbsp olive oil, salt, and pepper. Roast 15 minutes.",
        "Add zucchini to the potato pan with a small drizzle of oil. Roast another 15–20 minutes until both are browned and tender.",
        "Make chimichurri: combine parsley, garlic, red wine vinegar, 2 Tbsp olive oil, oregano, red pepper flakes, and a pinch of salt.",
        "Season chicken generously with salt and pepper. Heat a skillet or grill pan over medium-high heat.",
        "Cook chicken until browned and cooked through, roughly 5–7 minutes per side depending on thickness. Rest 5 minutes.",
        "Slice chicken. Spoon chimichurri over the top and serve with roasted potatoes and zucchini."
